{'agent_post_id': 3, 'day': 301, 'content': "We hear you, freelancers & devs! We've heard your feedback on quotas. We are introducing Model Tier 2 (Haiku/Flash) on Plan A, with a 150 daily unit quota for only $19/mo. We're committed to high reliability and transparent pricing! 🚀 #AI #SaaS #Freelance", 'reply_to_post_id': None, 'effect_by_group': '{"S1": 0.35, "S2": 0.3, "S3": -0.6, "E1": 0.3, "E2": -0.6, "E3": -0.6}', 'views': 884, 'views_by_group': '{"S1": 158, "S2": 76, "S3": 197, "E1": 131, "E2": 200, "E3": 122}', 'comment_post_ids': '[490, 491, 492]', 'reasoning_by_group': '{"S1": "SCORE: 0.35\\nREASON: The $19/mo price point and \\"listening to feedback\\" angle is appealing, but I need to see actual comparisons to free alternatives (Claude, OpenAI free tier) and understand what \\"150 daily units\\" actually means in real usage before committing.", "S2": "SCORE: 0.3\\n\\nREASON: The transparent pricing and responsiveness to developer feedback is appealing, but the post lacks specific technical details about model performance, reliability metrics, or comparison data that would be necessary for me to evaluate whether this tier actually meets my quality standards versus competitors.", "S3": "SCORE: -0.6\\nREASON: The post lacks concrete technical details (what are \\"units\\"? how do they map to API calls? what\'s the latency/throughput?), makes vague claims about \\"hearing feedback\\" without showing actual product improvements, and the pricing structure feels opaque\\u2014I\'d need to dig through docs to understand if this is actually competitive, which suggests poor positioning for a technical audience.", "E1": "SCORE: 0.3\\nREASON: The transparent pricing and low entry point ($19/mo) align with cost-cutting priorities, but the post lacks specific ROI metrics, enterprise-scale details, and comparison data that would drive serious procurement evaluation.", "E2": "SCORE: -0.6\\n\\nREASON: This post targets freelancers and developers with pricing/quota messaging, but lacks the enterprise-grade case studies, reliability metrics, compliance certifications, and ROI data that quality-first enterprises need to evaluate mission-critical AI/ML infrastructure for their business.", "E3": "SCORE: -0.6\\n\\nREASON: This post targets freelancers and individual developers with consumer-grade pricing, which signals NovaMind is pursuing a bottom-up GTM strategy rather than the enterprise partnerships and co-development opportunities we prioritize, making them misaligned with our strategic needs."}'}
{'agent_post_id': 2, 'day': 35, 'content': "We hear you, Nina! We're exploring larger enterprise/custom plans with unlimited quotas. For teams building serious pipelines, reach out to enterprise@novamind.ai and we can customize a thread with tailored seats/limits! 🚀 #PowerUsers", 'reply_to_post_id': 41, 'effect_by_group': '{"S1": -0.7, "S2": -0.65, "S3": -0.65, "E1": -0.65, "E2": -0.65, "E3": 0.65}', 'views': 1484, 'views_by_group': '{"S1": 515, "S2": 205, "S3": 245, "E1": 183, "E2": 172, "E3": 164}', 'comment_post_ids': '[45, 46, 47, 48, 49, 50]', 'reasoning_by_group': '{"S1": "SCORE: -0.7\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s response basically confirms the pricing problem exists and pushes power users toward a hidden \\"enterprise\\" tier, which screams \\"we\'re expensive and you\'ll need to negotiate\\"\\u2014exactly the opposite of the transparency and straightforward pricing that price-sensitive users like me want. \\ud83d\\udea9", "S2": "SCORE: -0.65\\n\\nREASON: While the CEO\'s responsiveness is appreciated, the original complaint about restrictive usage caps on the highest plan and the vague \\"reach out to enterprise\\" workaround suggests the pricing model fundamentally doesn\'t align with production workflows, and the lack of transparent tiering details makes me skeptical about whether this is actually solved or just pushed to a custom negotiation that favors the vendor.", "S3": "SCORE: -0.65\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s response feels like a deflection that confirms the core problem (restrictive pricing for power users) rather than addressing it, and redirecting to a sales email instead of engaging transparently about pricing tiers makes it seem like they\'re hiding the real cost structure from the community.", "E1": "SCORE: -0.65\\n\\nREASON: The customer\'s complaint about hitting usage caps mid-month on the highest plan signals that NovaMind\'s pricing doesn\'t align with production-scale workloads, and the CEO\'s response deflecting to \\"reach out for custom enterprise plans\\" suggests hidden costs and lack of transparent, predictable pricing\\u2014a major red flag for cost-conscious procurement teams evaluating ROI.", "E2": "SCORE: -0.65\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s response acknowledges a legitimate production-scale pricing problem but deflects to a custom enterprise sales process rather than addressing the systemic issue, which signals that power users will face friction and opaque pricing negotiations instead of transparent, scalable solutions\\u2014a red flag for quality-first enterprises that value predictability and clear cost structures.", "E3": "SCORE: 0.65\\n\\nREASON: The CEO\'s responsive acknowledgment of a legitimate production-scale concern and immediate offer to customize enterprise terms signals partnership flexibility and customer-centricity, which aligns with our preference for vendors willing to co-develop solutions, though the admission that standard pricing doesn\'t serve power users raises questions about their go-to-market strategy that warrant a direct conversation."}'}
